My latest attempt (dwarven arch) has had some amusing pet incidents.  I knew
something weird was going to happen when I saw a whistle in the very first
room, picked it up, and discovered that it's magic.  I like magic whistles.
A lot.  Makes robbing shops so much easier (as well as going down stairs,
etc., etc.)

So I make it down to minetown; my starting kitten, Fuzzbutt, has become a
large cat.  Very nice.  As I'm working on clearing out the book store, a
small dog comes and starts to make a pest of himself, so I chucked a spare
food ration at him.  Two pets and a magic whistle means the shop's cleared
fairly quickly, and I go off to the priest to buy some protection.

On the way, Fuzzbutt decides to take on the watch captain and dies.  Darn.
Oh, well--at least I still have the dog; I think I'll call him Miner, in
honor of where I found him.

So I go back to the main dungeon looking for Sokoban.  Several levels down,
a pony starts to attack me.  I toss him a spare lichen corpse, and keep
moving.  Run into a soldier ant, whistle for my pets.  That's odd, only the
pony shows up--where's Miner?  As I'm going back over the level, I found
out--near where I last saw him, I step on a level-teleport trap and wind up
back on level 1.  I make my way back down to the pony, but I don't see any
sign of Miner along the way...*sigh*.

Now, I'm just waiting to tame a fourth pet and watch the pony die/disappear
on me shortly afterwards...the RNG is having fun with my pets.  :-)



